ibition silently breaks existing call sites that perform the now-outlawed behavior'","Prompt bucket definitions: MIGRATED='the plan already updates this site to satisfy the new prohibition'; EXEMPTED='carves this site out of the prohibition'; UNCOVERED='the site performs the outlawed behavior' (lines 24-27)","Worked example (line 19-21) is prohibition-only: 'require tests to pass before merge → grep for gh pr merge'. For an ADDED obligation (a schema field / required argument existing sites must now satisfy) the invisible set is sites that do NOT YET SATISFY the obligation — semantically inverted from 'performs the outlawed behavior'."],"finding":"The plan widens T13's TRIGGER to fire on additive obligations but keeps the MIGRATED/EXEMPTED/UNCOVERED classification and enumeration protocol body unchanged, yet that body is written exclusively in prohibition terms ('now-outlawed behavior', 'site performs the outlawed behavior', 'satisfy the new prohibition'); the decision rule is no longer co-located with the case (additive obligation) it will now fire on.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f39754e5d23eac437","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → P2; src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T13.md lines 16-30 (ENUMERATE/CLASSIFY body)","norm_id":"n1b98542cfc973ddd","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A plan adds a required argument to a shared helper; the executor runs T13 (now triggered on the obligation) but the classification protocol tells it to grep for 'call sites of the behavior being outlawed' — there is no outlawed behavior, so the executor either abstains via fail-open or produces no obligation-side finding, defeating the widening.","A plan adds a schema-field invariant every writer must uphold; UNCOVERED as defined ('site performs the outlawed behavior') never matches a site that simply fails to satisfy the new obligation."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In plan_review_T13.md, generalize the 