definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the unchanged det-gate pre-filter actually fires on additive-obligation plans that carry NO enforcement verb (e.g. 'add required argument --foo', 'field X all sites must populate'); if it can skip such plans, either widen the T13 regex to cover additive-obligation vocabulary or state in the plan why those plans are acceptably out of scope.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'it is a skip-only pre-gate and already fires on obligation vocabulary (\"now needs|requires\", require\\w*, \"prerequisite\", \"precondition\"), so the LLM router remains the applicability authority.'","det_gate_rules.py:20-25 (module docstring): the pre-gate 'PRE-FILTERS ... a plan skips a criterion only on TOTAL subject-vocabulary absence; ... A not-fired gate performs zero LLM routing for that criterion' — so a plan whose obligation is phrased without the listed tokens never reaches the widened prompt.","The T13 regex (det_gate_rules.py:112) is centered on prohibition/enforcement vocabulary (block/reject/enforce/deny/gate/cannot-merge/require-before); an additive obligation like 'add required argument --foo' or 'all callers must populate field X' need not contain now-needs/requires/require*/prerequisite/precondition."],"finding":"The plan widens T13's LLM prompt/router to additive obligations but deliberately leaves the deterministic pre-gate regex unchanged, justifying this by claiming the pre-gate 'already fires